<title>USA: Motorola Inc Q4 net falls, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Motorola Inc Q4 net falls, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>SCHAUMBURG, Ill. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.39		    $0.72</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.39		     0.72</p>
<p> Net			238,000		  432,000</p>
<p> Revs		   7,685,000		7,298,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     609,000		  609,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     609,600		  609,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call consensus estimate for 1996 Q4 earnings was $0.41 a share, with a range of $0.35 to $0.45.  </p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.90		    $2.93</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 1.90		     2.93</p>
<p> Net		    1,154,000		1,781,000</p>
<p> Revs		  27,973,000	     27,037,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     609,000		  609,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     609,600		  609,800</p>
<p>	 (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 results include &quot;tens of millions of dollars&quot; of restructuring costs, as well as other unusual charges for the period, resulting in a combined negative impact to pre-tax earnings of more than $150 million.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
